- `action(n1, "start the process")`: Hallucinates a behavior not present in the source; the description begins directly with `"reviewing the received application"` without an intermediate starting action (violates SMC1/SMC2).
- `action(n12, "end process")`: Hallucinates a behavior not present in the source; the description concludes immediately after `"write back the case data"` with no separate ending action described (violates SMC1/SMC2).
- `precedence(i1, n1)` / `precedence(n1, n2)`: Breaks exact source chronology by inserting an undocumented node between the process initiation and the first documented step, `"reviewing the received application"` (violates SMC3).
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Fails to faithfully reflect source responsibilities; the text explicitly assigns all tasks to `"the review clerk"`, whereas the model uses a generic `"Default"` participant (violates SMC7).